      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the maximum for ibuprofen, so I want to check with you first.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times a day is 6400 mg/day. That's double the usual prescription maximum of 3200 mg/day, and four times the typical OTC limit of 1200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high significantly raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and heart problems, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis could be a typo for a standard regimen, for example:\n- 400 mg PO QID (1600 mg/day). The 1600 may have been meant as the daily total.\n- 600 mg PO QID (2400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO TID (2400 mg/day) or 800 mg PO QID (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nWhich dose and frequency did you mean? Once you tell me, I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1600 mg QID, please confirm and give the clinical reason so I can include it in the order note. A dose this far over the maximum will probably also need a pharmacy review."
      }
     ],
